### Scope (how changed, exit criteria untouched)
- Router `skills/paper/SKILL.md` (~50 lines): frontmatter; the register
  question (moved from submission-event); the procedures shared by every
  stage written once: provenance (authentic artifact at its source, one
  `sha256sum` line beside the frozen copy), landing-page link check on the
  version, delegation wording for `/update-publist` that reads true before
  and after ticket 1484 ("load it and follow its gates; if the runtime
  refuses the load, ask the author to type it"); one backticked
  `references/<event>.md` pointer per stage (`tests/test_skill_reference_pointers.py:27`).
- Five references, same skeleton each: Registers · Provenance · Filesystem ·
  Outward gates (who clicks) · Delegates · Author-only (ask, do not drop) ·
  Done when. Entry types are never written in /paper: "type per
  `/update-publist`'s status table" (books, talks and chapters follow the
  same lifecycle; `accepted` names "contract signed" as the book trigger).
  Two folder conventions named, never merged: the paper repo's
  `release/<date>/` (tracked text, ingest-decision-letter) and the
  `papiers/` dated folder (frozen authentic outputs, CNRS convention).
  Repo-side bookkeeping stays in each checklist (submission branch, git tag
  per event, STATE); a dataset deposit (Zenodo) with related identifiers is
  an Author-only ask item at `published`.
  Delegates: `/update-publist` (page, HAL), `/ingest-decision-letter`
  (decision-received), `/pdf-finish` (submitted, resubmitted, published),
  `/track-changes-pdf` (resubmitted), `/choose-venue` after a rejection.
- `published` reproduces the worked example step by step: dated release
  folder with publisher PDF and publication mail, hashed; `sent/` →
  `published/` move; hosted preprint swapped for the publisher PDF under the
  same filename when the licence allows (`/update-publist --page-only`, gate
  `make sync`, author confirms); bib entry per the status table; publisher
  HTML metadata checked against the PDF; HAL version via `/update-publist
  --hal-only`; roadmap row; DOI landing-page check; author-only: Zotero
  indexing of supporting material, co-authors informed, Zenodo related
  identifiers, release-journal entry.
- No helper script (YAGNI: `sha256sum`, `ingest_letter.py archive`).
- Rename sweep, one commit: delete `skills/submission-event/`; edit
  `skills/choose-venue/SKILL.md:15`, `skills/conference-submission-prep/SKILL.md:67`,
  `rules/README.md:125`, `tests/test_rules_resident_budget.py:39`; `make
  skills-catalog`; add `submission-event` to RETIRED in
  `tests/test_retired_skill_names.py` (the one existing guard for "no alias").
  Historical records (`design/audits/`, `memory/evidence/`, `health/journal.jsonl`)
  untouched. Projection symlinks are refreshed by `idh install`
  (`adapters/lifecycle.py:83-88` creates `paper`, `:233-258` prunes the
  dangling `submission-event`), on padme and doudou after merge.

### Constraints for the coder
- Skills resident budget 6282 of 6300 (`tests/test_resident_census.py:65`;
  a card counts `len(name)+len(description)`, current card 261): `paper` plus
  its description ≤ 279 chars, description ≤ 274; aim lower, 1485 will need
  headroom too.
- `check-agnostic.sh` rejects `/home/[a-z]`: write `~/CNRS/...`.
- Frontmatter free text quoted (`tests/test_skill_frontmatter.py:145`); no
  dragon vocabulary in the description's first sentence
  (`tests/test_skill_descriptions.py:23`).

### Exit criterion 4 (dry run) on padme
Padme can evidence criteria 1, 2 and 5. Criterion 3 is evidenced as a text
trace: a table mapping each worked-example step of this ticket to a line of
`published.md`. Criterion 4 is run on padme as the same walk against the data
paper's facts in this ticket (one row per step: done / to do / author-only,
with the evidence kind each row would take), reported in the merge-request
body and labelled a padme text-trace. The live positive control runs on
doudou: sync the harness, `idh install`, then `/paper <data paper> published`;
the merge request carries those instructions.

### Questions queued for the author (raid continues on the defaults)
1. Who runs the live dry run on doudou, and when? Default: the author, after
   merge, per the instructions in the merge request.
2. Is "nothing to do except HAL" still the expected answer? Ticket 1484 logs a
   HAL SWORD PUT on hal-05570600 v3 on 2026-11-09, likely this paper. Default:
   the checklist is written for the general case; the expected row set is
   reported as found.
3. Did the 2026-11-09 release update Zenodo 19236130's related identifiers,
   and is a git tag per event part of the convention? Default: both listed as
   Author-only ask items, not as done steps.
4. Can the How-to 44 text be supplied, or located on doudou? Default: the
   `accepted` HAL step is marked "confirm against How-to 44".

### Later review
Observe only. At the next real manuscript event (for instance a decision on
the Oeconomia Varia submission of 2026-03-18): did the agent need a step
absent from the checklist? Record in the CNRS journal; reopen on evidence.

### Blind-Spot verdict
Four material omissions, all folded above (tags and Zenodo registers; entry
types owned by `/update-publist`; `/pdf-finish` and `/track-changes-pdf`
delegates; `idh install` before the doudou dry run). Resident budget, rename
consumers, other-project mentions, name clash: checked clean.

